\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The centered symbol}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Over the real numbers let #{f_j(r)=\sin\bigl(\tfrac{2\pi r_j}{N_j}\bigr)} be the centered symbol, with periods
#{N_j\ge 3}. By \ref{fdip-0142} the zeros of the interpolated map are the products of
coordinate zeros: #{0} is a sample, and the zero corresponding to #{\pi} is a sample
when #{N_j} is even and the midpoint of the straddling edge when #{N_j} is odd.
An odd period therefore gives a zero on an edge with no zero vertex. Thus #{\tilde f}
is [resolved](fdip-015I) if and only if every #{N_j} is even.}
